          "entradaId": "freeman-65",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Under the impression that the word kesitah, here rendered “pieces of money,” means a lamb, many of the ancient commentators supposed that here was an evidence of early coinage; the “pieces of money” being coins having on them the impress of a lamb. Stanley (Hist. Jewish Church, L…"
      }
